Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,The Moon is moving away from Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.40,0:00:06.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,About 3.8 centimeters every year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.40,0:00:09.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,The reason? Ocean tides.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.50,0:00:14.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,Earth's rotation pulls the tidal bulge ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.20,0:00:18.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,That tug transfers energy into the Moon's orbit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.30,0:00:22.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,Scientists bounce lasers off reflectors on the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.10,0:00:27.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,They time the light's return to measure the distance.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.00,0:00:33.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,A tiny drift—about as fast as fingernails grow.
